            {
                "entry_id": "99c51acf-fb9f-36af-9700-045eb5543fd3",
                "word": "mongoloid",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "04dabd0a-8b95-4825-93d3-4570256ff799",
                        "entry_id": "99c51acf-fb9f-36af-9700-045eb5543fd3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "mongoloids"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "238787dc-c320-35ee-83b3-ac105cfd186e",
                        "entry_id": "99c51acf-fb9f-36af-9700-045eb5543fd3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A member of the racial classification of humanity composed of peoples native to North Asia, East Asia, Southeast Asia, Pacific Oceania, the Americas, and parts of Central Asia and South Asia (and sometimes eastern Fennoscandia) – as well as their descendants in other parts of the world."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8b676e7-3cb9-4c14-b58e-736d11eb9c6c",
                                "sense_id": "238787dc-c320-35ee-83b3-ac105cfd186e",
                                "text": "Both American Indians and Mongoloids have shovel-shaped incisor teeth and, at birth, display the Mongoloid spot — a blue spot above the rump, which fades within a short time; many also have the Mongoloid, or epicanthic, fold of the inner part of the upper eyelid."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e315eb6b-3b2a-43d6-9565-54b0728bdb21",
                                "sense_id": "238787dc-c320-35ee-83b3-ac105cfd186e",
                                "text": "On the average, he found caucasoids to have the longest heads and mongoloids the roundest; mongoloids the straightest hair and negroids the most tightly curled; caucasoids the narrowest noses and negroids the broadest."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a55b1a5-20d9-4f25-be74-2e96cb559036",
                                "sense_id": "238787dc-c320-35ee-83b3-ac105cfd186e",
                                "text": "As before, the genetic distance between Caucasoid and Mongoloid is the smallest and that between Negroid and Mongoloid is the largest."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0df70630-8c47-37ff-90ec-457740c20769",
                        "entry_id": "99c51acf-fb9f-36af-9700-045eb5543fd3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person with Down syndrome."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "offensive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6fe1d0b-8626-4c6d-a8f1-ad97b11c03f6",
                                "sense_id": "0df70630-8c47-37ff-90ec-457740c20769",
                                "text": "Kirman (1953) drew attention to some physicians' reluctance to offer even ordinary and routine medical care to mongoloids, whose treatment they consider a waste of time."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5c9b01b-7b3c-4d87-adb3-fff1c273e341",
                                "sense_id": "0df70630-8c47-37ff-90ec-457740c20769",
                                "text": "It is therefore of interest to examine hospital records of mongoloid children with heart defects in order to find out how frequently operations are performed upon these children."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6cac3def-751d-46ff-9cd8-7867dc8e3ab5",
                                "sense_id": "0df70630-8c47-37ff-90ec-457740c20769",
                                "text": "The operation made each feature, itself, look O.K., but her overall looks are still those of a Mongoloid. Her facial expression immediately reveals that she is different. She still has that peculiar look. You can see she has Down's syndrome."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "97e50fed-2ed5-3755-a5af-8b8ab490f835",
                        "entry_id": "99c51acf-fb9f-36af-9700-045eb5543fd3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An idiot, a retard; a general term of abuse, due to association with Down syndrome."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "derogatory",
                            "offensive",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
